king":0},"body":"my query:\r\n\r\n```\r\n/createWorkspace a vscode extension that uses the SecretStorage API to set an API Key\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere's the generated package.json:\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n\t\"name\": \"my-extension\",\r\n\t\"displayName\": \"My Extension\",\r\n\t\"description\": \"A vscode extension that uses the SecretStorage API to set an API Key\",\r\n\t\"version\": \"1.0.0\",\r\n\t\"publisher\": \"my-publisher\",\r\n\t\"engines\": {\r\n\t\t\"vscode\": \"^1.60.0\"\r\n\t},\r\n\t\"categories\": [\r\n\t\t\"Other\"\r\n\t],\r\n\t\"activationEvents\": [\r\n\t\t\"onCommand:my-extension.setApiKey\"\r\n\t],\r\n\t\"main\": \"./out/extension.js\",\r\n\t\"contributes\": {\r\n\t\t\"commands\": [\r\n\t\t\t{\r\n\t\t\t\t\"command\": \"my-extension.setApiKey\",\r\n\t\t\t\t\"title\": \"Set API Key\"\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t]\r\n\t},\r\n\t\"scripts\": {\r\n\t\t\"vscode:prepublish\": \"npm run compile\",\r\n\t\t\"compile\": \"tsc -p ./\",\r\n\t\t\"watch\": \"tsc -watch -p ./\"\r\n\t},\r\n\t\"devDependencies\": {\r\n\t\t\"@types/node\": \"^16.7.13\",\r\n\t\t\"typescript\": \"^4.4.3\",\r\n\t\t\"vscode\": \"^1.60.0\"\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nCouple problems:\r\n1. I'm not sure what `\"vscode\": \"^1.60.0\"` is... it should be `@types/vscode` and also 1.60 is a pretty old version\r\n2. it includes `\"onCommand:my-extension.setApiKey\"` but that activation event isn't needed anymore so it generates a Problem in VS Code\r\n3. The generated `extension.ts` file doesn't seem to know about the SecretStorage API at all... maybe it's too new of an API... I wanna say it was added in the like 1.50s though\r\n\r\nPossible side note: If we do go down the route of having `/createWorkspace` \"be smarter\" for certain workflows/languages, I would love if extension dev was one of those.","closed_by":{"login":"bhavyaus","id":25044782,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MDQ0Nzgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25044782?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus","html_